# KGM agent workspace rules

This folder is the local control plane for shared Agent assets.

## Boundaries

- Portable source lives only in `content/skills`, `content/settings`, and `content/subagent`.
- Credentials, authentication, private memory, backups, receipts, and machine state live only in `state/` and never enter Git.
- Generated caches and host-specific runtime files are not source.
- Do not scan the whole home directory. Extend the registered host inventory deliberately and test it.
- Do not resolve conflicting assets by guessing. Stop and ask the owner.
- The Kimi bridge may return only Skill manifests, allowlisted shared rule documents, and Markdown persona/subagent files under `content/`. It must never read `state/`, `.kimi`, or runtime configuration.
- Do not commit, add a remote, push, or publish without separate user approval.

## Maintenance

- Add a Skill with `control/bin/new-skill.sh`.
- Rebuild the Skill index with `python3 -B control/bin/rebuild-claude-md.py`.
- Validate Skills with `bash control/bin/validate-skills.sh`.
- Repair only missing links with `bash control/bin/link-local.sh`; it refuses to replace unexpected paths.
